From 5b9e97e06ed776f100974b2ec59875a946a40474 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OrientCOMPASS <316423573+OrientCOMPASS@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 03:33:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] btif_media: decode AAC (FDK/LATM) and LDAC (libldacdec)
 sink streams (data plane)

btif_media_task.c could only decode SBC A2DP sink streams.  Wire the two
new codecs into the existing rx pipeline (RxSbcQ + 20 ms decode tick):

* decoder reset dispatches on codec_info[2]: SBC keeps the OI path,
  AAC opens an FDK aacDecoder in TT_MP4_LATM_MCP1 mode (RFC 3016
  payloads), LDAC heap-allocates a libldacdec instance.  Both create the
  AudioTrack from the parsed CIE sample rate / channel mode.
* inc-media handler branches per active codec:
  - AAC: aacDecoder_Fill over the whole RTP payload, then drain
    aacDecoder_DecodeFrame until AAC_DEC_NOT_ENOUGH_BITS; PCM sized by
    CStreamInfo frameSize*numChannels.
  - LDAC: skip the 1-octet media payload header (low nibble = frame
    count, same layout as SBC), then ldacDecode() per frame using the
    returned bytesUsed; frameSamples*channels 16-bit PCM out.
* the enque pump stamps num_frames=1 for AAC (LATM has no media payload
  header, so its first octet must not be interpreted as a frame count)
  and the decode tick drains whole packets for AAC/LDAC instead of using
  the SBC per-frame budget.
* clear_track releases the FDK handle / libldacdec instance and resets
  the active-codec state to SBC.
---
 btif/src/btif_media_task.c | 402 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 401 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

